  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% accuracy while image (resnet50) achieves only 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant signal modality. Uncertainty: We have no information on whether multiprofile aggregation improves the RNA representation, and this is the single most impactful untested design axis for the dominant modality. This experiment (config_002: rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is a clean single-variable extension of config_001—only the profile setting changes from single to multi, with the simplest aggregation (avgpool)—isolating the effect of multi-profile aggregation on RNA performance. It is the best use of the next budget slot because: (1) it directly extends the strongest baseline, (2) it tests a fundamental data-structure question (does having multiple profiles help?) before committing to more complex choices like transformer aggregation or learned encoders, (3) if multiprofile helps, it opens a productive exploitation path (test transformer aggregation, then combine with better encoders); if it does not, it efficiently rules out that axis and redirects budget toward encoder choice. Testing multimodal fusion or image improvements before establishing the best RNA configuration would be premature given the large modality gap."
}

